WEBVTT

NOTE Captions mirror the on-screen text of «Tu ou vous ?» (Leçon 4). Times follow the fragment timecodes of fork-tu-ou-vous.mp4.

00:00.000 --> 00:05.500
French has two words for "you": tu and vous.

00:06.000 --> 00:15.500
tu — one person you're close to: friends, family, children.

00:16.000 --> 00:26.500
vous — one person you don't know well: strangers, older people, shops and work.

00:27.000 --> 00:32.500
And for two or more people it's always vous.

00:33.000 --> 00:37.500
The verb follows: tu as · vous avez. Not sure? Say vous.

00:38.000 --> 00:39.900
À vous ! — Your turn.

00:40.000 --> 00:47.900
Exactly. Stranger → vous. Vous → avez.

00:48.000 --> 00:55.000
One question: do you know this person well?

00:55.500 --> 01:03.000
No → vous: « Excusez-moi, vous avez l'heure ? »

01:03.500 --> 01:10.500
Yes → tu: « Salut, tu as l'heure ? »

01:11.000 --> 01:17.900
They travel in pairs: tu as · vous avez. Never mix them.

01:18.000 --> 01:25.000
Samedi, 10 h. You meet Camille at a café.

01:25.500 --> 01:33.000
Camille is an old friend. « Tu veux un café ? » — one friend → tu.

01:33.500 --> 01:40.000
Then Léo joins you.

01:40.500 --> 01:49.000
Now there are two of them.

01:49.500 --> 01:52.900
À vous ! — Your turn.

01:53.000 --> 02:00.900
Oui ! More than one → vous. Always.

02:01.000 --> 02:07.000
Vous has two jobs.

02:07.500 --> 02:14.000
1 — polite: one person you don't know well.

02:14.500 --> 02:21.000
2 — plural: two or more people, whoever they are.

02:21.500 --> 02:26.500
Camille → tu veux. Camille + Léo → vous voulez.

02:27.000 --> 02:30.900
Count first. Then ask how well you know them.

02:31.000 --> 02:38.000
Two or more people → vous.

02:38.500 --> 02:45.000
One person, close to you → tu.

02:45.500 --> 02:51.000
One person, not sure → vous.

02:51.500 --> 02:55.900
À bientôt !
